const e="RISK DISCLOSURE STATEMENT\n\nThis Risk Disclosure Statement (the “Statement”) applies to the electronic trading platform, websites and mobile applications of {{WEB_NAME}} (the “Platform”) and should be read together with the Platform’s Terms of Use and applicable product rules. References to products or services in this Statement apply only where those products or services are actually available to you on the Platform.\n\nBefore using the Platform, you should understand the risks of digital asset transactions and independently assess whether they are suitable for your experience, financial resources and ability to bear losses. {{WEB_NAME}} does not provide personalised investment advice through this Statement. This Statement cannot describe every risk. You may lose all the digital assets in your account and, in some market conditions, be unable to close a position. Seek independent professional advice if you do not understand a product or its risks.\n\n1 Risks Relating to Digital Assets\n\n1.1 The price and value of digital assets, and any income from them, may fluctuate significantly and move against your interests. An asset may lose all its value. Buying and selling digital assets may result in losses rather than profits; historical performance does not guarantee future results.\n\n1.2 Do not assume that a digital asset has legal tender status, government backing or commodity reserves. These characteristics depend on the asset and applicable law. Assets such as Bitcoin and Ether rely on network protocols and cryptography; their prices are not guaranteed by a central bank. Protocol changes, governance decisions and security weaknesses may affect their operation and value.\n\n1.3 Digital asset transactions may be irreversible. Assets lost through fraud, an incorrect address, an unsuitable network or an accidental transfer may be impossible to recover. Check the asset, network, address and required payment information before submitting a transfer.\n\n1.4 Submitting a transaction does not mean that it has been confirmed on the blockchain. The time recorded on a public ledger may differ from the time you initiated it. Network congestion and confirmation requirements may delay deposits, withdrawals and settlement.\n\n1.5 The value of an asset depends in part on the continuing willingness of market participants to buy or exchange it. If demand or liquidity disappears, you may be unable to sell it, or may have to sell at a substantial loss. Its value may be permanently reduced to zero.\n\n1.6 Digital assets are exposed to fraud and cyberattacks. Technical problems affecting {{WEB_NAME}}, wallets or blockchain networks may prevent you from accessing, transferring or trading your assets.\n\n1.7 Market bubbles and loss of confidence can cause sharp price changes. Changes to software, government action, competing assets, inflation or deflation, theft, exposure of private information and interruption of transaction processing may reduce confidence and demand.\n\n1.8 An account balance on {{WEB_NAME}} should not be treated as a bank deposit. The legal treatment of your assets depends on the applicable laws and the nature of the relevant service.\n\n1.9 Do not assume that digital assets held in your account are covered by bank deposit insurance or an investor compensation scheme. Check whether any protection applies to the specific product and your jurisdiction before trading.\n\n2 Risks Relating to Derivatives, Margin and Digital Asset Borrowing\n\n2.1 Where derivatives or leveraged trading are available, a small change in the underlying asset’s price may produce a much larger gain or loss. An adverse movement may require additional margin or a reduction of your position. If applicable margin requirements are not met, positions may be forcibly liquidated and you may lose all of your margin.\n\n2.2 Financing a transaction with collateral may expose you to losses exceeding the collateral you initially deposited. You may need to provide additional collateral or pay interest at short notice. If you fail to meet the applicable requirements, collateral or positions may be liquidated at a loss under the relevant product rules. Consider your financial position and investment objectives before using such financing.\n\n2.3 Where digital asset borrowing is available, the required collateral may change with the market value of the borrowed assets and the collateral. You may need to add collateral or repay a loan within a short period. Failure to do so may trigger disposal of collateral or other measures specified in the applicable agreement. Review borrowing costs, repayment obligations and liquidation conditions before borrowing.\n\n2.4 Do not rely on receiving a margin call or other warning before liquidation. Under the applicable product rules, automated risk controls may act before you receive or respond to a notification. You may be unable to choose the position, timing or order of liquidation. Monitor your own margin and exposure; {{WEB_NAME}} does not undertake through this Statement to advance funds or replenish your margin.\n\n3 Other Risks\n\n3.1 Changes in laws, regulatory requirements or enforcement practices may affect the holding, transfer, trading and value of digital assets. The availability of a service does not establish that it is lawful or suitable in every jurisdiction. You should understand the requirements that apply to you.\n\n3.2 Legal or regulatory changes may require {{WEB_NAME}} to restrict, suspend or discontinue services or account functions. This may prevent you from trading or accessing assets when you wish and may result in losses or additional obligations.\n\n3.3 Electronic trading relies on hardware, software, communication networks and third-party infrastructure. Failures or interruptions may affect order routing, matching, execution, recording and settlement. An order may be delayed, not executed or executed differently from your instructions. Internet connections and displayed information may also be delayed; take these limitations into account when managing your positions.\n\n3.4 Proceeds from selling digital assets and other income may be subject to taxes, withholding, duties or other charges. The rules and their interpretation may be uncertain, change over time or have retrospective effect. You are responsible for understanding and fulfilling your applicable reporting and payment obligations and should seek independent tax advice where necessary.\n";export{e as default};
